---
import Analytics from '../components/Analytics.astro'
import { appUrl, guideUrl, siteRoot } from '../home/paths'
import '../theme.css'
import '../home/home.css'

// Two services and what each one is for. Short on purpose.
const REPO = 'https://github.com/cmdcolin/bender'
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${siteRoot}favicon.svg`} />
    <title>Privacy — bender</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="bender uses Google Analytics to count visits and Firebase to hold your saved voices. Nothing else."
    />
    <Analytics />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="bar">
      <div class="barIn">
        <a class="brand" href={siteRoot}>bender</a>
        <nav class="barNav" aria-label="Site">
          <a href={guideUrl}>User guide</a>
          <a href={REPO}>Source</a>
        </nav>
        <div class="barEnd">
          <a class="btn primary" href={appUrl}>Open the app →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="head">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="pitch">
        bender runs in your browser. Two outside services are involved, and this
        page is the whole list.
      </p>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2 class="secHead">Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Counts visits: which pages get opened, roughly where from, and on what
          sort of device. It sets cookies to do that. Any tracker blocker
          switches it off, and everything here works the same without it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2 class="secHead">Firebase</h2>
        <p>
          Only if you sign in. Google handles the sign-in, and one Firestore
          document holds your saved voices: a name, and the board it stands for,
          spelled the same way a shared link spells it. The same document holds
          the board you last had open, so the home page can offer it back. Stay
          signed out and there is no document at all.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2 class="secHead">Getting rid of it</h2>
        <p>
          <b>×</b> in the saved menu deletes a voice on the spot. To have the whole
          document deleted, say so in
          <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>an issue</a>. Nothing is sold and there are
          no ads.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
